      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-270103",
        "knowledge_point_id": "db6e4cf3-803a-5942-9ce0-7047942e078a",
        "knowledge_point": "Computing an Arcsine Integral by Completing the Square",
        "problem": "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{-12-x(x+12)}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12-x(x+12) & =-12-({x}^{2}+12x) \\\\  & =-12-({x}^{2}+12x+36-36) \\\\  & =-12-((x+6)^{2}-36) \\\\  & =24-(x+6)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{-12-x(x+12)}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{24-(x+6)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{24(1-(x+6)^{2}/24)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{24}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+6)^{2}/(2\\sqrt{6})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+6)/2\\sqrt{6})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+6}{2\\sqrt{6}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+6}{2\\sqrt{6}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{6}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-6-\\sqrt{6}$ | $-6+\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{-12-x(x+12)}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{-6-\\sqrt{6}}^{-6+\\sqrt{6}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+6)/2\\sqrt{6})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}u. \\\\  & =15{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =15(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =15(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =5\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
