        "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-78568: left-multiplication by A^{-1}, then B, gives x=BA^{-1}d; matrix order matters. q-104536: the system gives (x,y,z)=(2,1,0), so the sum is 3. q-80197: cot(x)=0 gives x=±90 degrees, whose numerical product is -8100. q-114918: substituting u=(6x+1)/2 gives the factor 1/6. q-114926: u=2x-7 gives twice the inverse-secant antiderivative. q-114910: completing the square gives (x-3)^2+9 and the stated inverse-tangent antiderivative. q-270103: the radicand is 24-(x+6)^2; substitution gives 15 times the arcsine difference between -1/2 and 1/2, hence 5π. q-19532 and q-114928: completing the squares gives (x-6)^2-1 and (x-4)^2-1, respectively, yielding the stated inverse-secant antiderivatives with the standard absolute-value derivative convention. q-10061, q-10064, and q-10143: the chain rule verifies the respective factors -1/2, -1/9, and 1/7. q-13533: u=2x^2 transforms the integral to (5/4) times the integral of cos(u) from 0 to π, which is zero. q-28595: the graph decreases, passes through (0,4), and approaches y=5 from below as x tends to negative infinity; current option 1 is equivalent to MA's annotated solution image, although the image paths differ. q-117799: the asymptote spacing is 4π/3, so B=3/4; the midpoint height gives D=-3, hence B+D=-9/4. q-42663: arccos has range [0,π], so 3π is excluded. No earlier submission or grade is supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
